{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the [foreigners' children].</b> (ibid.), he mentioned the eunuchs before the children of the foreigner, because he completed with them, for so is the way of Scripture: \"and I will give to Isaac Jacob and Esau, and I will give to Esau\" (Joshua 24:4):" "<b>To serve Him.</b> Service of HaShem is to do His statutes:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {0 "The bracketed [הנכר] and gloss (שם) meaning 'ibid.' appear in the source; the lemma as cited is truncated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:47.733278108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}